# short-description: Ultima gauge cluster image: stock boot/root + ext4 /data
# long-description: Adds a small ext4 /data partition (p3) to meta-ti-bsp's
# stock sdimage-2part-efi.wks.in, same as ultima-beagleplay.wks.in for the
# original board — see that file for the full history/reasoning (p1 must
# stay the vfat --source bootimg-efi partition, root stays partition #2,
# --no-fstab-update on root, resize_rootfs.service masked in
# tisdk-base-image.bbappend). Every line here is generic TI/EFI wic-plugin
# syntax (${TI_WKS_BOOTLOADER_APPEND}, ${EFI_PROVIDER}, bootimg-efi source),
# nothing AM625-specific, so this is a straight copy for BeagleY-AI
# (AM67A/J722S) rather than a real port — kept as a separate per-machine
# file instead of sharing WKS_FILE across both machines only to match this
# layer's existing one-file-per-machine convention.
#
# Hardware-verified 2026-08-29 (board in hand): the ROM does find
# tiboot3.bin in p1 the same way as beagleplay-ti's GP boot, resolving the
# caveat this header used to carry. Two real fixes landed the same day, both
# found by booting for real over serial (see beagleplay-falcon/NOTES.md
# "Resolved: the hang was never a hang — display works end to end" for the
# full story, including a red-herring "hang" that was actually just missing
# console=/earlycon, not a real freeze):
#
# 1. `dtb=k3-am67a-beagley-ai.dtb` sourceparam below. Without it,
#    bootimg-efi's grub.cfg has no `devicetree` line, and GRUB/the EFI stub
#    silently falls back to whatever minimal internal control DTB U-Boot
#    itself was using — which has `main_i2c1` (the bus carrying this
#    board's it66122 HDMI bridge chip) disabled and no bridge node at all,
#    since U-Boot doesn't need HDMI for its own operation. Confirmed by
#    diffing /sys/firmware/fdt off the live kernel against both candidate
#    DTBs — it matched U-Boot's, not this build's. With the sourceparam,
#    bootimg-efi (see oe-core's bootimg-efi.py `_copy_additional_files` /
#    `do_configure_grubefi`) both copies the real kernel-target dtb onto
#    this FAT partition and adds `devicetree /k3-am67a-beagley-ai.dtb` to
#    grub.cfg for us — no separate IMAGE_BOOT_FILES or grub.cfg bbappend
#    needed, this one sourceparam does both.
# 2. `console=ttyS2,115200n8 earlycon` added to the bootloader append
#    below. Same UART instance name TI's own am64xx.inc hardcodes into
#    TI_WKS_BOOTLOADER_APPEND for that family — j722s/k3.inc's own default
#    is empty (`?=` ""), so this board got no console= at all before. Not
#    just cosmetic: without earlycon specifically, a from-cold boot with
#    the correct (fuller) devicetree above produces zero serial output at
#    all even though the kernel boots fine — looks exactly like a hard
#    hang and easy to misdiagnose as one (this project did, briefly).
#
# Confirmed end to end on real hardware, including one fully unattended
# reboot straight through autoboot (no manual U-Boot intervention): main_i2c1
# registers, the it66121 HDMI bridge chip probes, tidss initializes DRM and
# creates /dev/fb0, ultima-splash succeeds, and ultima-app renders real
# frames (first frame ~1.2s after launch, stable, zero crashes).
#
# 2026-08-29, later same day: `quiet` + `vt.global_cursor_default=0` added
# below. TI Falcon boot mode was investigated as the big fast-boot lever
# (same as BeaglePlay), but is a dead end on this SoC specifically: TI's own
# ti-falcon Yocto wiring only covers am62xx/am62axx/am62pxx/am62xx-lp, and
# more fundamentally, TI has never published the TIFS stub firmware
# (ti-fs-stub-firmware-j722s-*) the Falcon fast-path needs to do its
# security handshake — confirmed absent on every branch tip of TI's
# ti-linux-firmware repo (re-checked live, including a branch updated 12
# days before this note). Not a missing-config problem, a
# TI-hasn't-shipped-it problem — see beagleplay-falcon/NOTES.md "Falcon on
# J722S/BeagleY-AI: dead end" for the full trail. With Falcon off the
# table, the console=ttyS2 line just above is the same synchronous
# 115200-baud UART bottleneck BeaglePlay had before its own `quiet` fix
# (measured there at ~3.3s/~38KB of console text on the critical path
# before tidss inits, plus systemd's own [ OK ]/Started spam, which `quiet`
# also suppresses). `vt.global_cursor_default=0` hides the blinking fbcon
# text cursor on the HDMI output between tidss coming up and ultima-app
# taking the framebuffer (same fix BeaglePlay and RPi5/Buildroot carry).
# Not yet re-measured on this board's own boot-log capture — do that before
# calling this win closed.

bootloader --timeout=3 --append="rootfstype=ext4 console=ttyS2,115200n8 earlycon quiet vt.global_cursor_default=0 ${TI_WKS_BOOTLOADER_APPEND}"
part --source bootimg-efi --sourceparams="loader=${EFI_PROVIDER},dtb=k3-am67a-beagley-ai.dtb" --fstype=vfat --label boot --active --align 1024 --use-uuid --fixed-size 128M
part / --source rootfs --fstype=ext4 --label root --align 1024 --use-uuid --no-fstab-update
part /data --fstype=ext4 --label data --fixed-size 16M --align 1024
